>
>About one out of every ten or so games I can get a character about that
>strong, if I'm lucky...
>
>What's the trick with getting super-studboy characters???

Well, there's no one particular trick. What you have to do is, try and
figure out what normally leads to your deaths. For a lot of people it's
sailing merrily into combat and not keeping an eye on their hit points.
Others aren't cautious enough when it comes to testing out unidentified
items (ever put on a cursed pair of lev. boots?). Others always go into
the Gnome mines too early and get trounced. So, just think, how is it
that you usually (or often) die? And what can you do about it?

My personal bit of advice is, alway always ALWAYS be aware of what
stuff you've got stashed in your pack. If you ever die with a wand
of teleportation or digging, or a scroll of teleportation, like I
used to do because I forgot I had them, you're an idiot! Remember
what offensive wands you have, and don't hesitate to use them! Learn
how to identify wands by engraving with them.. all the offensive wands
can be IDed this way. If you're really desperate to escape from a
bad situation, try reading a spellbook - it might wrench you away.
That's saved my life a couple of times as a last resort.

Oh, and telepathy is very VERY important for avoiding bad fights.
If you don't know how to get it - eat a Floating Eye corpse, and then
find a towel or blindfold - when you Apply the blindfold or Put on
the towel, you can mind-scan all the [intelligent] monsters on the
level! Life-saving!

